{"name":"Blue Prince","hex":"#6a808f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"prince","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (male) ruler, a sovereign; a king, monarch. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A female monarch."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To behave or act like a prince.","To transform (someone) into a prince."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prince"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Prince","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Prince is a puzzle adventure game developed by Dogubomb and published by Raw Fury. It was released on April 10, 2025, for PlayStation 5, Windows and Xbox Series X/S systems, with a later release for macOS on September 29, 2025, and Nintendo Switch 2 on March 3, 2026."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/Blue_Prince_cover_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Prince","wikidata":"Q125131501"},{"title":"Blue Prince (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Prince is a 2001 album by the Belgian Jazz guitarist Philip Catherine. He was accompanied by Hein van de Geyn Hans Van Oosterhout (drums) and Bert Joris The album was well received by Jazz critiques, rosing Catherine's performance and saying that \"one of the finest guitarists on the globe.\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7f/Blue_Prince.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Prince_(album)","wikidata":"Q4929642"},{"title":"Prince","blocks":[{"text":"A prince is a male ruler or a male member of a monarch's or former monarch's family. Prince is also a title of nobility, often hereditary, in some European states. The female equivalent is a princess. The English word derives, via the French word prince, from the Latin noun prīnceps, from primus (first) and caput (head), meaning \"the first, foremost, the chief, most distinguished, noble ruler, prince\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Prince_William_attends_Holocaust_Memorial_Day_%2854290704867%29%28cropped_3%29.jpg/330px-Prince_William_attends_Holocaust_Memorial_Day_%2854290704867%29%28cropped_3%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince","wikidata":"Q2747456"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Tonda_Ros_-_GDC_Awards_2026.jpg/500px-Tonda_Ros_-_GDC_Awards_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://